```tsx
export function LobbyScreen({
  players,
  secondsRemaining,
  map,
}: {
  players: { name: string; race: string; mmr: number; ready: boolean }[]
  secondsRemaining: number
  map: { name: string; imageUrl: string; spawns: { x: number; y: number }[] }
}) {
  const urgent = secondsRemaining <= 5
  const warning = secondsRemaining <= 15

  const raceColor = (race: string) =>
    ({ terran: '#4fc3f7', protoss: '#ce93d8', zerg: '#aed581', random: '#ffb74d' }[race] ?? '#90a4ae')

  return (
    <Container>
      <TopRow>
        <TimerZone>
          <Overline>
            <PulseDot animate={{ opacity: [1, 0.3, 1] }} transition={{ duration: 2, repeat: Infinity }} />
            Match found · locking in
          </Overline>
          <TimerText
            $urgent={urgent}
            $warning={warning}
            key={secondsRemaining}
            initial={{ scale: urgent ? 1.08 : 1 }}
            animate={{ scale: 1 }}
            transition={ANIM_SPRING}
          >
            0:{String(secondsRemaining).padStart(2, '0')}
          </TimerText>
        </TimerZone>

        <PlayerList>
          {players.map((p, i) => (
            <PlayerRow key={p.name} $ready={p.ready}
              initial={{ opacity: 0, x: 24 }}
              animate={{ opacity: 1, x: 0 }}
              transition={{ ...ANIM_SPRING, delay: i * 0.1 }}>
              <RaceBadge style={{ background: `${raceColor(p.race)}22` }}>
                <span style={{ color: raceColor(p.race), fontWeight: 700, textTransform: 'capitalize' }}>
                  {p.race[0]}
                </span>
              </RaceBadge>
              <div>{p.name}</div>
              <MmrBadge $high={p.mmr >= 2000}>{p.mmr} MMR</MmrBadge>
            </PlayerRow>
          ))}
        </PlayerList>
      </TopRow>

      <MapPreview>
        <img src={map.imageUrl} alt={map.name} style={{ width: '100%', height: '100%', objectFit: 'cover', opacity: 0.85 }} />
        {map.spawns.map((s, i) => (
          <SpawnPoint key={i} style={{ left: `${s.x}%`, top: `${s.y}%` }}
            initial={{ scale: 0, opacity: 0 }}
            animate={{ scale: [0, 1.4, 1], opacity: 1 }}
            transition={{ ...ANIM_SPRING, delay: 0.6 + i * 0.25 }} />
        ))}
        <div style={{ position: 'absolute', bottom: 12, left: 16, ...overline, textTransform: 'uppercase', letterSpacing: '0.15em' }}>
          {map.name}
        </div>
      </MapPreview>
    </Container>
  )
}
```

## Key design decisions

1. **Timer as hero** — 120px tabular numerals, color-shifting (white → `amber400` → `red400`) following the draft-screen urgency pattern. The per-second `key` change triggers a scale pop; at ≤5s it gets a noticeable 1.08 spring.
2. **Staggered entrance** — players and spawn points animate in sequence (0.1s / 0.25s offsets), giving the lobby a 'roster assembling' rhythm instead of popping in all at once.
3. **Race identity through color** — each race gets a tinted badge at 13% opacity with matching text color, using race-adjacent hues; swap to your exact race color tokens from `colors.ts`.
4. **MMR as quiet flex** — tabular numerals, amber for high ratings, muted otherwise. Confident but not shouting.
5. **Negative space does the work** — the flex-1 timer zone against the fixed-width roster creates tension; nothing is cramped.

**Production notes:** use the actual race icon set rather than letter badges, wire `soundIntegration` like `post-match-dialog.tsx` for the final-5-seconds tick, and replace hardcoded colors with the design-system semantic tokens (`--theme-positive`, race colors from `colors.ts`), which I've approximated inline here.

Here's a rebuilt typography system for your poetry journal, following the typeset guidance:

**Font pairing (2 families, genuine contrast):**
- **Display/headings & poem titles:** Cormorant Garamond (elegant literary serif that fits a poetry journal far better than Papyrus)
- **Body, bylines & UI text:** Source Sans 3 (humanist sans for readability, real contrast with the serif)

Load with `display=swap` and only the weights you use: 400, 600 (serif also 500 italic for titles).

**Type scale (1.333 ratio, rem-based to respect user settings):**

```css
:root {
  --font-serif: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
  --font-sans: 'Source Sans 3', 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif;

  --text-caption: 0.875rem;   /* 14px */
  --text-body:   1.0625rem;   /* 17px */
  --text-byline: 1rem;        /* 16px, small caps */
  --text-title:  clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
  --text-h1:     clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
}

h1 {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-h1);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
}

.poem-title {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: var(--text-title);
  font-weight: 500;
  font-style: italic;
  line-height: 1.2;
}

.byline {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: var(--text-byline);
  font-weight: 400;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;   /* open tracking for small caps */
  color: #555;
}

body {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: var(--text-body);
  line-height: 1.65;
  font-weight: 400;
}

.poem-body {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: 1.25rem;
  line-height: 1.7;
  max-width: 34em;          /* short lines suit verse */
}

.pull-quote {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  font-weight: 500;
  font-style: italic;
  line-height: 1.3;
  max-width: 30ch;
  padding-left: 1.25rem;
  border-left: 3px solid currentColor;
}

.caption {
  font-family: var(--font-sans);
  font-size: var(--text-caption);
  color: #666;
}
```

**What this fixes:**
- **Papyrus heading** → literary serif with real personality and tight display tracking
- **11px body** → 17px, comfortably readable, 1.65 line-height
- **Inverted bylines/titles** → bylines are now quiet small-cap labels; poem titles dominate in large italic serif
- **Undifferentiated pull quotes** → large italic serif with a rule and constrained measure, clearly featured
- **Arbitrary sizes** → one consistent scale combining size + weight + family + style so hierarchy reads at a glance
- **Measures & rhythm** → `ch`/`em` max-widths keep lines in the 45–75 character comfort zone

**Verification checklist:** headings vs. titles vs. bylines distinguishable instantly ✓ · body ≥16px ✓ · same roles styled identically everywhere ✓ · only 2 families, 4 weights ✓ · rem units keep zoom accessible ✓ · WCAG AA contrast on grays (#555/#666 only for secondary text) ✓
